scenario.en:
Read this function and state, in one sentence, the business rule it implements:<br/><pre><code>function flushCart(cart, now) {
  if (cart.items.length === 0) return;
  const idleMs = now - cart.lastTouchedAt;
  if (Math.floor(idleMs / 60000) &lt; 30) return;
  db.exec(`DELETE FROM carts WHERE id='${cart.id}'`);
  events.emit('cart.expired', { id: cart.id });
}</code></pre>What is the rule, and which lines forced you down to machine level to find it?

